  "type": "numerical",
  "level": 1,
  "question": {
    "text": "<p>If the acceleration due to gravity experienced by a point mass at a height <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>h</mi></math>&nbsp;above the surface of earth is same as that of the acceleration due to gravity at a depth <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>&#945;</mi><mi>h</mi><mfenced><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>&#8810;</mo><msub><mi>R</mi><mi>e</mi></msub></mrow></mfenced></math> ) from the earth surface. The value of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>&#945;</mi></math> will be _____ .</p><p>(use&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>R</mi><mi>e</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>6400</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>km</mi></math>)</p>",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [],
  "correctValue": "2",
  "solution": {
    "text": "<blockquote><p>Acceleration due to gravity at a height <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>h</mi></math>&nbsp;above the earth&#39;s surface is given by&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>g</mi><mfenced><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>-</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>2</mn><mi>h</mi></mrow><msub><mi>R</mi><mi>e</mi></msub></mfrac></mrow></mfenced></math>&nbsp;</p><p>And&nbsp;acceleration due to gravity at depth <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>d</mi></math> below the earth surface is given by&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>g</mi><mfenced><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>-</mo><mfrac><mi>d</mi><msub><mi>R</mi><mi>e</mi></msub></mfrac></mrow></mfenced></math>.</p><p>As&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>g</mi><mi>above</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>g</mi><mi>below</mi></msub></math></p><p>So,&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>g</mi><mfenced><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>-</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>2</mn><mi>h</mi></mrow><msub><mi>R</mi><mi>e</mi></msub></mfrac></mrow></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mi>g</mi><mfenced><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>-</mo><mfrac><mi>d</mi><msub><mi>R</mi><mi>e</mi></msub></mfrac></mrow></mfenced></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8658;</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>2</mn><mi>h</mi></mrow><msub><mi>R</mi><mi>e</mi></msub></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mi>d</mi><msub><mi>R</mi><mi>e</mi></msub></mfrac></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8658;</mo><mi>&#945;</mi><mi>h</mi><mo>=</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">d</mi></math></p><p>Thus, the value of&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>&#945;</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn></math>.</p></blockquote>",
